       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). The 1,600 mg single dose is also twice the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise substantially.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth, three times daily**, a common regimen for pain\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf the dose is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. Otherwise, tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
